Warning 10 in paper.tex line 56: Solo `)' found.
Three obstacles prevent today\u2019s samplers from meeting these emerging constraints. 1) Importance scores\u2014whether attention weights or gradient norms\u2014are obtained during the forward pass that just ended, therefore they are already stale when the next batch is sampled; the effect is amplified on dynamic graphs. 2) Diversity-promoting samplers such as k-DPPs need a similarity kernel whose construction becomes the new wall-clock and memory bottleneck at \(10^6\) nodes or beyond. 3) Energy accounting usually stops at the GPU, so published \"green AI\" numbers are not comparable across machines with different CPU or PCIe usage.  
                                                                                        ^
